'''brenthian''' (bren′thi-a̤n), ''n.'' and ''a.'' [< ''Brenthus'' + ''-ian''.] '''I.''' ''n.'' A beetle of the genus ''Brenthus''.

'''II.''' ''a.'' Of or pertaining to the genus ''Brenthus''.

'''brenthid''' (bren′thid), ''n.'' A beetle of the family ''Brenthidæ''.

'''Brenthidæ''' (bren′thi-dē), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Brenthus'' + ''-idæ''.] A family of rhynchophorous coleopterous insects, related to the ''Curculionidæ''. {{smaller|They are of an elongate form, and have long snouts and moniliform antennæ. The genera are numerous.}}

